  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Npc237962 and SCCH-26 through multiple target-mediated pathways. Npc237962 is implicated in the target of two distinct compounds: Ancistrobenomine A and dimethyl (1S,9R,15S,16S,17S,18R,21R)-15,17,18-trihydroxy-2,12-diazahexacyclo[14.2.2.19,12.01,9.03,8.016,21]henicosa-3,5,7-triene-2,18-dicarboxylate, both of which are targeted by SCCH-26. This indicates that Npc237962 may interact with these compounds, which in turn inhibit SCCH-26. The shared target of these compounds and the direct interaction with SCCH-26 suggest a possible mechanism involving the inhibition of a common biological process, though the exact nature of this process remains unclear. The evidence is consistent with a mechanism involving the modulation of a cellular pathway, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the precise role of Npc237962 in this context.",
